#!/bin/bash
# tools/codex-live: the backlog loop in an interactive Codex session you watch live, as Claude Code's /loop. Codex is the coordinator
# (the zn-coordinate skill) and runs each worker as one of its own sub-agents, in its own worktree under .worktrees/; `codex agents`
# in another terminal browses the workers' sessions. tools/codex-loop is the headless variant. One coordinator at a time.
# Environment: ZN_CODEX_SANDBOX (default danger-full-access: workspace-write keeps .git read-only),
# ZN_CODEX_MODEL (default gpt-6-astra). Fast tier for the owner-requested backlog work.
set -u
cd "$(dirname "$0")/.." || exit 2
[ -f .paused ] && { echo "codex-live: .paused exists, remove it first (zn-resume)"; exit 1; }
[ -d .logs/codex-loop/lock ] && { echo "codex-live: tools/codex-loop is running (.logs/codex-loop/lock): stop it first"; exit 1; }
mkdir -p .worktrees
exec codex -C "$PWD" -s "${ZN_CODEX_SANDBOX:-danger-full-access}" -a never --search -m "${ZN_CODEX_MODEL:-gpt-6-astra}" \
  -c service_tier=fast -c features.fast_mode=true -c agents.max_threads=5 -c sandbox_workspace_write.network_access=true --add-dir "$HOME/.zinc" --add-dir "$HOME/Library/Caches/ccache" \
  "You are the coordinator of the Zinc backlog team. Follow the zn-coordinate skill and keep going until .paused exists or nothing is left; never ask the owner a question.
Run each worker as one of your sub-agents: create its worktree with 'git worktree add -b work/<first-id> .worktrees/<first-id> develop', brief it as the skill's section 'Brief' says, and tell it to run every command inside that worktree and to work its tasks with the zn-start skill.
Use the available worker slots for independent chains, including workers that do not build. At most two building workers at once. Heavy commands queue themselves with tools/work-run SECONDS COMMAND; do not wait for a coordinator token. When a worker returns, integrate its branch (section 'Integrate'), then choose, claim and start the next chain.
Start now: check 'git worktree list' and that no other coordinator runs, then choose and claim."
